{
  "study_id": "wikitable_reasoning_protocol_v2",
  "description": "Reasoning scaffold/style matrix for table benchmarks. Every reasoning style is carried by one flexible visible reasoning field; v2 adds pairwise style coalitions under that same trace carrier.",
  "preview_path": "Obsidian/Transferability/Project/coding_agent_logs/codex/code/systematic_design/reasoning_scaffold_and_style/wikitable_reasoning_protocol_v2_preview.html",
  "protocol": {
    "factory_reference": "factory/cards/themes/reasoning-trace.md defines the general visible trace: reasoning must bind to concrete query inputs such as table cells, claim parts, schema columns, or prior-turn answers.",
    "scaffold_axis": "Single general visible carrier: scaffold.trace. It gives the model one reasoning field plus the benchmark's normal final field.",
    "reason_axis": "Reasoning style/procedure. In this v2 manifest every style run is paired with scaffold.trace so the model emits reasoning before the final field.",
    "design_reason": "Prior WTQ runs suggest evidence-style visible scaffolds help more than plan-only scaffolds. V2 tests vanilla visible trace, single styles, and pairwise style coalitions while keeping the output carrier fixed."
  },
